# UIKit Development Standards

**For universal anti-patterns:** See `general-llm-anti-patterns.mdc`
**For Swift language, layers, concurrency:** See `swift-5-9-development-standards.mdc` or `swift-6-development-standards.mdc` (project language mode)
**For HIG and Liquid Glass:** See `ios-ui-development-focus.mdc` (SwiftUI examples; HIG rules apply to UIKit too)
**Reference:** <https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit>; Xcode `uikit-app-modernization` skill (`xcrun agent skills export`)—link only, do not vendor

**Forbidden:** Inventing UIKit API names; gating code on an OS version without `#available` matching the project deployment target; claiming UI works without building and running (see `ios-build-automation.mdc`).

## API Availability (verify against deployment target)

|API|Introduced|Fallback below floor|
|---|---|---|
|Cell registrations, list configurations, content configurations|iOS 14|`register(_:forCellWithReuseIdentifier:)`|
|`UIButton.Configuration`, `keyboardLayoutGuide`, `reconfigureItems`|iOS 15|Manual button styling, keyboard notifications, `reloadItems`|
|`UIHostingConfiguration`|iOS 16|`UIHostingController` child|
|`registerForTraitChanges`, `contentUnavailableConfiguration`|iOS 17|`traitCollectionDidChange` (deprecated)|
|Automatic Observation tracking|iOS 18 opt-in (`UIObservationTrackingEnabled` Info.plist key), default iOS 26|Manual `didSet` → update|
|`updateProperties()`, `.flushUpdates`, `UIGlassEffect`, `UIButton.Configuration.glass()`|iOS 26|`viewWillLayoutSubviews` (tracked on iOS 18)|
|Scene life cycle required to launch|iOS 27 SDK builds|None: adopt scenes|

