## 1. App Structure (CRIT)

### 1.1 Scene-Based Life Cycle (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** UIKit apps own windows in a `UIWindowSceneDelegate`; apps built with the iOS 27 SDK without scenes fail to launch.

❌ Bad: `func application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:) { window = UIWindow(frame: UIScreen.main.bounds) }`
✅ Good: `func scene(_ scene: UIScene, willConnectTo: UISceneSession, options: UIScene.ConnectionOptions) { guard let ws = scene as? UIWindowScene else { return }; window = UIWindow(windowScene: ws) }`
⚠️ Why: Launch assertion on iOS 27 SDK; no multi-window, iPad resizing, or iPhone Mirroring support
🔧 Fix: Add `UIApplicationSceneManifest` to Info.plist; move UI-state callbacks (`applicationDidBecomeActive`, etc.) to scene equivalents; keep app delegate for process-level setup
📍 See: TN3187 <https://developer.apple.com/documentation/technotes/tn3187-migrating-to-the-uikit-scene-based-life-cycle>

**Detect:** No `UIApplicationSceneManifest`, `UIWindow(frame:)` in app delegate, `applicationWillResignActive` doing UI work, missing launch screen key (`UILaunchScreen` / `UILaunchStoryboardName`)

### 1.2 No Global Screen/Window State (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** Read geometry and environment from the current view, window, scene, or trait collection, never from process-wide singletons.

❌ Bad: `UIScreen.main.bounds.width`, `UIApplication.shared.windows.first`, `UIApplication.shared.keyWindow`
✅ Good: `view.bounds.width`, `traitCollection.displayScale`, `view.window?.windowScene?.screen`
⚠️ Why: Wrong values with multiple windows, iPad resizing, external displays, and resizable iPhone apps
🔧 Fix: Pass context in; use `traitCollection` for scale/size class; `UIScreen.main` is deprecated (iOS 26)
📍 See: Section 3.3 (size classes)

**Detect:** `UIScreen.main`, `UIApplication.shared.windows`, `keyWindow`, `statusBarOrientation`, `UIDevice.current.orientation` for layout

