## 4. Lists and Collections

### 4.1 Diffable Data + Cell Registrations (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** New lists use `UICollectionView` with diffable data sources, cell registrations, and compositional layout.

❌ Bad: `func collectionView(_:numberOfItemsInSection:)` + `dequeueReusableCell(withReuseIdentifier: "Cell")` + `reloadData()` after edits
✅ Good: `let reg = UICollectionView.CellRegistration<UICollectionViewListCell, Item.ID> { cell, _, id in ... }`; apply `NSDiffableDataSourceSnapshot`
⚠️ Why: Index-path crashes (`NSInternalInconsistencyException`), no animations, string reuse IDs
🔧 Fix: Snapshot of stable IDs (not full models); `reconfigureItems` for content changes; `UICollectionLayoutListConfiguration` for table-like lists

**Detect:** `UITableViewDataSource` in new code, string reuse identifiers, `reloadData()` after single-item change, snapshots of mutable model structs, `performBatchUpdates` with manual index math

### 4.2 Content Configurations

❌ Bad: `cell.textLabel?.text = item.title` (deprecated cell properties)
✅ Good: `var c = cell.defaultContentConfiguration(); c.text = item.title; cell.contentConfiguration = c`
⚠️ Why: Deprecated; no state-based styling; no automatic Dynamic Type
🔧 Fix: `UIListContentConfiguration` or `UIHostingConfiguration` (SwiftUI cell content); `contentUnavailableConfiguration` for empty states

**Detect:** `textLabel`, `detailTextLabel`, `imageView` on cells, custom empty-state overlay views

