## 5. View Controllers

### 5.1 Child Containment

❌ Bad: `view.addSubview(child.view)` (no containment calls)
✅ Good: `addChild(child); view.addSubview(child.view); child.didMove(toParent: self)`; reverse: `willMove(toParent: nil)`, `removeFromSuperview()`, `removeFromParent()`
⚠️ Why: Child misses appearance callbacks, traits, rotation, safe areas

**Detect:** `addSubview(*.view)` without `addChild`, missing `didMove(toParent:)`, removal without `removeFromParent()`

### 5.2 Retain Cycles in Closures

❌ Bad: `button.addAction(UIAction { _ in self.save() }, for: .primaryActionTriggered)`
✅ Good: `UIAction { [weak self] _ in self?.save() }`; `registerForTraitChanges` handlers receive `self` as parameter (no capture needed)
⚠️ Why: View controller never deallocates; tasks and observers keep running
🔧 Fix: `[weak self]` in stored closures (actions, registrations, timers, notifications); verify `deinit` fires with Memory Graph

**Detect:** `self.` in `UIAction`, `CellRegistration`, `Timer`, `NotificationCenter` closures without weak capture, missing `deinit` log in debug

### 5.3 Task Lifetime

❌ Bad: `override func viewDidLoad() { Task { for await x in stream { label.text = x } } }` (unowned, never cancelled)
✅ Good: Store `loadTask = Task { [weak self] in ... }`; cancel in `viewDidDisappear(_:)`
⚠️ Why: Leaks, stale UI updates, wasted work after dismissal
🔧 Fix: Own and cancel tasks; UI types are `@MainActor`, so no `DispatchQueue.main.async` hops in Swift 6 code
📍 See: `swift-6-development-standards.mdc` concurrency sections

**Detect:** Fire-and-forget `Task {` in view controllers, `DispatchQueue.main.async` in `@MainActor` types, UI mutation from `Task.detached`

