## 8. SwiftUI Interop

❌ Bad: Rebuilding a SwiftUI screen in UIKit (or vice versa) to avoid bridging
✅ Good: `UIHostingController(rootView:)` as child VC; `UIHostingConfiguration` in cells; share state via one `@Observable` model
⚠️ Why: Duplicate UI, divergent state
🔧 Fix: Contain hosting controllers per §5.1; size with `sizingOptions = .intrinsicContentSize` when embedded

**Detect:** `UIHostingController.view` added without `addChild`, duplicated view logic across frameworks, two sources of truth for one screen

---

## Final Verification

Build and run on a simulator; resize (iPad windowing), rotate, set largest Dynamic Type, toggle Dark Mode, run VoiceOver on new screens. Then run `swift-5-9-brutal-audit.mdc` or `swift-6-brutal-audit.mdc`.
